+
+
+## 2026-11-10 telemetry query correction
+
+The collector previously spawned nvidia-smi every sample (2s CLI timeout, 3s
+freshness). A stale sample and subsequent TimeoutExpired stopped the 2026-11-10
+Goal attempt. The underlying reason for that CLI delay remains unknown.
+
+Only the Linux metric query is changed: nvml_metrics.py holds one read-only NVML
+handle, with a single-GPU check and memory-counter validation. Sample UTC is the
+oldest observation/start, not query completion. gpu_query_seconds and
+gpu_source=nvml_persistent are recorded. No new Python dependency is installed.
+The launch pin manifest includes the helper. Rollback files and exact diff are
+archived in the 2026-11-10 telemetry-goal-loop research record.
+
+No query retry, CLI fallback or last-good reuse is implemented. NVML is also the
+underlying library for nvidia-smi, so it is not an independent emergency sensor.
+An error publishes invalid and exits; a blocked call stops advancing snapshots
+and the unchanged external freshness/heartbeat guards terminate the workload.
+All memory thresholds, 3s freshness and owned-process cleanup remain unchanged.
+
+Short validation: 40 paired idle reads (direct median0.85ms, CLI58.5ms), 6 Python
+checks, 10 native freshness counterexamples, invalid/frozen producer termination
+integrations and the existing no-model smoke gates. This is not unattended
+reliability acceptance, nor proof that driver stalls can never occur.
+
+Final late-success refusal: after the real run and cleanup, V2 added a 2s
+completed-sample budget (mirroring the former CLI deadline). A returned late call
+publishes invalid and exits, rather than being overwritten by a fast successor.
+A blocked C call is still covered externally by the unchanged3s freshness gate;
+the helper does not pretend to preempt it. Virtual2.1/3.1s cases fail onV1 and
+pass onV2. V2 repeated no-model guards, not another complete model run.
